text In a vacant classroom, after school.
text There, we kiss, just as we always do.
text The sun is dazzling as it sets.
text I embrace her strongly, trying to be as close to her as possible.
text I...
text I realize I'm still conflicted about this.
text About what I should be doing, if I really love Tomoyo.
text What kind of outcome should I be wishing for?
text Will things really be all right as they are?
text Am I supposed to start living a normal and decent life, so that I may be with Tomoyo?
text Or am I supposed to stand in her way here?
text I pull back my lips.
text Tomoyo's face is even redder than normal, probably due to the setting sun.
text I slip my hand up under Tomoyo's jacket.
text I want to be with Tomoyo.
text Just those feelings alone... I know they aren't a lie.
text They are feelings so strong that they make me conflicted, and start disregarding everything I thought was true.
text I lift Tomoyo up and throw her down on the desk.
text The door opens with a click.
text I... couldn't jump back.
text Without any panic at all, I look over my shoulder.
text If it was a student, I could just threaten them.
text However, unfortunately, the eyes I meet are those of a teacher.
text Yeah... this would end up closing it down entirely...
text Tomoyo's path to the student council, that is.
text Thinking this, I spontaneously make way toward the teacher.
text Even faster than I could think.
text So that Tomoyo's path wouldn't be closed off.
